    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (80.08) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) serving as our primary anchors. **Kyle Tucker** draws a high-leverage matchup against Singer, where his 4.56 xERA advantage and favorable platoon split position him for a massive production day. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong park factor and an advantageous matchup against Gordon, whose 4.08 xERA offers the perfect opportunity for **Jackson Merrill** to exploit his high-contact ceiling from the #5 hole. **Miguel Vargas** also merits attention at 59.41; while the matchup against Valdez is technically a platoon disadvantage, the projection rewards **Miguel Vargas** for his high xwOBA and the potential for stolen bases against a slower delivery, keeping him in the high-marginal tier despite the tough opponent.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Henry Bolte** (39.65) serving as the closest cut from the active lineup. While **Henry Bolte** benefits from a premium leadoff spot, the combination of Rasmussen\u2019s elite 3.30 xERA and a poor park factor depressed his efficiency below our 40.0 floor, prioritizing the safety of our higher-floor starters. Elsewhere, **Liam Hicks** (45.58), **Josh Jung** (51.72), **Wade Meckler** (51.81), and **Luis Lara** (43.71) round out the squad. **Wade Meckler** is particularly well-positioned given the wind-out conditions at his venue, which provided the necessary bump to keep him in the lineup over bench options like **Tommy White** (35.08). With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** currently idle, we are carefully monitoring the remaining active pool to ensure we do not hit our game caps while maintaining our edge in the scarcity-driven stolen base category.",
